From 5fa30a48dd1bab5b21163f57223761aa841e2fa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:42:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 027/126] dns: log failed exchanges once per server, with a
 count every 10 s

A failed DNS exchange was not logged at all on most paths of 1.14 (the rule
path, and timeouts or closed connections on the path of clients), so a router
whose DNS server is down showed an empty log. 1.13, and 1.14 for other errors,
logged one line per query, twice on 1.13, which floods the log ring of a router.
Now the client logs a failed exchange where the server is known: the first
failure of a server at once with its query, then while the server goes on
failing one line every 10 s with the count and the last failure. A query its
caller gave up is not a failure. The router and the inbound do not log those
errors again.
---
 dns/client.go                  |  3 +-
 dns/client_failure_log.go      | 90 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dns/client_failure_log_test.go | 86 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dns/router.go                  | 12 +++--
 route/dns.go                   |  6 +--
 5 files changed, 188 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 dns/client_failure_log.go
 create mode 100644 dns/client_failure_log_test.go

